  (text_box "Wire style = confidence of each connection\ngreen solid      C  confirmed (traced on both sides, or measured)\nblue solid       V  seen on one side of the board in the photos\norange dashed    I  inferred from datasheet, marking or usual practice\nred dotted       U  unknown: pin exists, destination not traced\n\nNothing is C yet. Every connection still needs a continuity check." (at 15.24 149.86 0) (size 119.38 35.56) (stroke (width 0.1524) (type solid) (color 120 120 120 1)) (fill (type color) (color 255 255 225 1)) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid 5eed0893-82ba-45ed-a46e-476ee7c401a0))
  (text_box "How to read this schematic\n- One sheet per function. Power nets (+48V, +3V3, +1V15, GND) are global power ports.\n- Net names starting TBD_ are placeholders for pins whose destination is not traced yet.\n- Values come from part markings (EIA-96 codes decoded); unmarked parts show the package only.\n- Pinouts of G2401PR, the \"05U\" ESD arrays, SCT2622 and the PoE module chip are assumed.\n- Generated by gen_schematic.py; edit that, not the .kicad_sch files.\n- lx-is601f-nets.csv lists every pin with its net and confidence code." (at 144.78 149.86 0) (size 129.54 35.56) (stroke (width 0.1524) (type solid) (color 120 120 120 1)) (fill (type color) (color 255 255 225 1)) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid 343afa6a-684b-442c-8339-272e3445b95e))
  (text "Sources: photos in the project album; Motorcomm YT9215SCH datasheet V1.03; SCT2622 datasheet; KiCad 7 standard libraries." (at 15.24 195.58 0) (effects (font (size 1.4 1.4) italic) (justify left top)) (uuid 3ee73bcc-8890-402d-b7a0-6f7316ee5f6a))
